# NOTICE

## This project

`postgres-mcp-go` is an independent Go implementation of the interface and
behaviour of [crystaldba/postgres-mcp](https://github.com/crystaldba/postgres-mcp).
It is licensed under the MIT License; see [LICENSE](LICENSE).

It is not a fork and contains no code copied from that project. The search
algorithm, the health checks, the column extraction, the safe-SQL validator, and
all the Go code were written for this project.

## Material derived from crystaldba/postgres-mcp

The original is MIT licensed, copyright © 2025 Crystal Corp. Its licence text is
reproduced below, as the MIT terms require for material derived from it.

Two things here are derived from it:

- **The safe-SQL allowlists.** `internal/safesql/allowlist_gen.go` is generated by
  `tools/gen_allowlist.py` from that project's `safe_sql.py`, and transcribes its
  curated lists of allowed statement types, AST node types, function names, and
  extension names. Those identifiers are facts about PostgreSQL, but the selection
  of them is that project's, so the attribution is ours to keep. To refresh it:

  ```sh
  python3 tools/gen_allowlist.py <path>/safe_sql.py > internal/safesql/allowlist_gen.go
  gofmt -w internal/safesql/allowlist_gen.go
  ```

- **The interface.** The tool names, parameters, and output shapes are deliberately
  identical, so this server is a drop-in replacement for the Python one.

Deliberate differences are documented in `goPortAdditions` in
`internal/safesql/safesql.go`, and in `AGENTS.md` under "Deliberate deviations
from the skill defaults".

